Licence: MIT License (LICENSE.md in that repository)
Copyright (c) 2024 - present, Bereket Engida

The MIT grant covers that software and associated documentation files.
Their brand assets, marketing copy, Trusted By lists, Ask AI widget, and
sign-in demos were not copied. okengine content, the okengine mark and
wordmark, and the Manifest-derivation diagram are original to this project.

Two behavioural differences from upstream are worth recording, because they are
not oversights: our sidebar is driven by the Fumadocs page tree rather than a
hand-written contents array, so meta.json stays the only source of navigation
truth; and the changelog is parsed from the committed root changelog.md rather
than fetched from the GitHub releases API, so the site build is
deterministic and builds with no network.

React Bits (hero prism backdrop)
-------------------------------
`site/components/landing/prism-backdrop.tsx` adapts the `Prism` WebGL
background — the ray-marched prism SDF, its grade, and the ogl mount — from
React Bits:

  https://github.com/DavidHDev/react-bits

Upstream path:
  src/content/Backgrounds/Prism/Prism.tsx

Licence: MIT License (LICENSE in that repository)
Copyright (c) 2025 David Haz

Adapted, not copied verbatim: the prop surface is replaced by fixed okengine
tuning (desaturated, no hue shift — the YIQ hue matrix tints near-grey ink
green), the `lightMode` flag follows the live `dark` class, the render loop
re-measures its percentage-sized host, device pixel ratio is capped, and the
loop obeys `prefers-reduced-motion` by painting one frame with time frozen.

Problem-space diagram (concept only)
------------------------------------
The idea of arguing the problem with a tabbed panel whose first view is a
complete-graph mesh of infrastructure concerns ("problem space") comes from
third-party framework marketing diagrams of that shape. No code, markup, or
copy was taken: the geometry, node list, labels, and prose in
`site/components/landing/collapse-diagram.tsx` were written from scratch, and
the nodes are drawn from okengine's own `replaces` lists in
`site/lib/elements.ts`.
